It might be kind of neat if jesters were able to intentionally set
traps. Perhaps they could take the raw ingredients (a bunch of arrows,
a scroll of fire, a potion of sleep, etc...) and set them up to make a
trap. Other monsters, of course, would not know the trap was there,
and you could trick them into triggering it.

What about intrinsics? I think they should gain intrinsic searching at
some level, or perhaps sleep resistance (they're just too full of
energy to fall asleep easily). It might also be cool if they gained
inherent polymorph at some level. Perhaps they could only polymorph
into animals, or maybe only animals associated with "trickster" myths:
fox, coyote, jackal, raven, spider.
Speaking of animals, it would make sense if the "trickster" animals
had a chance of being generated peaceful. And I think that they should
start off with a fox or coyote as a pet.

